" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045767/state.json" "file_sha256" "e834a2341c6e1f18464a75d5fa46289659b30f3fc44107666214c011a5735328"} {"question" "q-105672" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j+R\\,k$ is a vector field on ${R}^{3}$ and the partial derivatives of the components of $F$ all exist, then the curl of $F$ is the vector field given by\n\n$$\ncurl\\,F=∇\\times F=|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ P & Q & R\\end{aligned}|.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{curl}\\,F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ {e}^{y+z} & 1 & xyz\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[\\frac{∂}{∂y}(xyz)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(1)]i-[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xyz)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}({e}^{y+z})]j+[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(1)-\\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{y+z})]k \\\\  & =(xz-0)i-(yz-{e}^{y+z})j+(0-{e}^{y+z})k \\\\  & =xz\\,i+({e}^{y+z}-yz)j-{e}^{y+z}\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate $\\text{curl}\\,F$ at the point $(2,1,-1),$ and obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\text{curl}\\,F)(2,1,-1) & =2(-1)\\,i+({e}^{1+(-1)}-1(-1))j-{e}^{1+(-1)}\\,k \\\\  & =-2\\,i+2\\,j-k.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045767/state.json" "file_sha256" "e834a2341c6e1f18464a75d5fa46289659b30f3fc44107666214c011a5735328"} {"question" "q-105672" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045767/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4dec808fbb78198391326e2601a173f95510b8bd3afbddce4d593ffa6479681a"} {"question" "q-105672" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045767/state.json" "file_sha256" "e834a2341c6e1f18464a75d5fa46289659b30f3fc44107666214c011a5735328"} {"question" "q-105672" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2\\,i+2\\,j-k"] ["math" "-2\\,k"] ["math" "-3\\,j+k"] ["math" "3\\,k"] ["math" "i-2\\,j+k"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045767/state.json" "file_sha256" "e834a2341c6e1f18464a75d5fa46289659b30f3fc44107666214c011a5735328"} {"question" "q-105672" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2\\,i+2\\,j-k"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045767/state.json" "file_sha256" "e834a2341c6e1f18464a75d5fa46289659b30f3fc44107666214c011a5735328"} {"question" "q-105698" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the vector field $F=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)\\,i+y{z}^{2}\\,j+(x-z)\\,k.$ Evaluate $∇\\times F$ at the point  $(2,-1,3).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045767/state.json" "file_sha256" "e834a2341c6e1f18464a75d5fa46289659b30f3fc44107666214c011a5735328"} {"question" "q-105698" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j+R\\,k$ is a vector field on ${R}^{3}$ and the partial derivatives of the components of $F$ all exist, then the curl of $F$ is the vector field given by\n\n$$\ncurl\\,F=∇\\times F=|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ P & Q & R\\end{aligned}|.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{curl}\\,F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y) & y{z}^{2} & (x-z)\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x-z)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(y{z}^{2})]i-[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x-z)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y))]j+[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y{z}^{2})-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y))]k \\\\  & =(0-2yz)i-(1-0)j+(0-\\frac{1}{x+y})k \\\\  & =-2yz\\,i-j-\\frac{1}{x+y}\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate $\\text{curl}\\,F$ at the point $(2,-1,3),$ and obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\text{curl}\\,F)(2,-1,3) & =-2(-1)(3)\\,i-j-\\frac{1}{2+(-1)}\\,k \\\\  & =6\\,i-j-k.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045767/state.json" "file_sha256" "e834a2341c6e1f18464a75d5fa46289659b30f3fc44107666214c011a5735328"} {"question" "q-105698" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045767/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4dec808fbb78198391326e2601a173f95510b8bd3afbddce4d593ffa6479681a"} {"question" "q-105698" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045767/state.json" "file_sha256" "e834a2341c6e1f18464a75d5fa46289659b30f3fc44107666214c011a5735328"} {"question" "q-105698" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2\\,i-3\\,j"] ["math" "-3\\,j+2\\,k"] ["math" "6\\,i-j-k"] ["math" "i+2\\,j+3\\,k"] ["math" "j-6\\,k"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045767/state.json" "file_sha256" "e834a2341c6e1f18464a75d5fa46289659b30f3fc44107666214c011a5735328"} {"question" "q-105698" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6\\,i-j-k"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045767/state.json" "file_sha256" "e834a2341c6e1f18464a75d5fa46289659b30f3fc44107666214c011a5735328"} {"question" "q-131336" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $F(x,y,z)=x{e}^{yz}\\,i+yz\\,j+{e}^{yz}\\,k,$ what is $\\text{curl}\\,F?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045767/state.json" "file_sha256" "e834a2341c6e1f18464a75d5fa46289659b30f3fc44107666214c011a5735328"} {"question" "q-131336" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j+R\\,k$ is a vector field on ${R}^{3}$ and the partial derivatives of the components of $F$ all exist, then the curl of $F$ is the vector field given by\n\n$$\ncurl\\,F=∇\\times F=|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ P & Q & R\\end{aligned}|.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{curl}\\,F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ x{e}^{yz} & yz & {e}^{yz}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[\\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{yz})-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(yz)]i-[\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{yz})-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(x{e}^{yz})]j+[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(yz)-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x{e}^{yz})]k \\\\  & =(z{e}^{yz}-y)\\,i-(0-xy{e}^{yz})\\,j+(0-xz{e}^{yz})\\,k \\\\  & =(z{e}^{yz}-y)\\,i+xy{e}^{yz}\\,j-xz{e}^{yz}\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045767/state.json" "file_sha256" "e834a2341c6e1f18464a75d5fa46289659b30f3fc44107666214c011a5735328"} {"question" "q-131336" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045767/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4dec808fbb78198391326e2601a173f95510b8bd3afbddce4d593ffa6479681a"} {"question" "q-131336" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045767/state.json" "file_sha256" "e834a2341c6e1f18464a75d5fa46289659b30f3fc44107666214c011a5735328"} {"question" "q-131336" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(x{e}^{yz}-z)\\,i+x{e}^{yz}\\,j-xz{e}^{yz}\\,k"] ["math" "(z{e}^{yz}-y)\\,i+(xy{e}^{yz}-z)\\,j-{x}^{2}{e}^{yz}\\,k"] ["math" "(z{e}^{yz}-y)\\,i+xy{e}^{yz}\\,j-xz{e}^{yz}\\,k"] ["math" "-y\\,i+xy{e}^{yz}\\,j+xz{e}^{yz}\\,k"] ["math" "z{e}^{yz}\\,i+xy{e}^{yz}\\,j-xz{e}^{yz}\\,k"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045767/state.json" "file_sha256" "e834a2341c6e1f18464a75d5fa46289659b30f3fc44107666214c011a5735328"} {"question" "q-131336" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(z{e}^{yz}-y)\\,i+xy{e}^{yz}\\,j-xz{e}^{yz}\\,k"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045767/state.json" "file_sha256" "e834a2341c6e1f18464a75d5fa46289659b30f3fc44107666214c011a5735328"} {"question" "q-131340" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the vector field $F={x}^{2}\\,i+xz\\,j+{z}^{2}\\,k.$ Evaluate $∇\\times F$ at the point  $(-2,-3,1).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045767/state.json" "file_sha256" "e834a2341c6e1f18464a75d5fa46289659b30f3fc44107666214c011a5735328"} {"question" "q-131340" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j+R\\,k$ is a vector field on ${R}^{3}$ and the partial derivatives of the components of $F$ all exist, then the curl of $F$ is the vector field given by\n\n$$\ncurl\\,F=∇\\times F=|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ P & Q & R\\end{aligned}|.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{curl}\\,F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ {x}^{2} & xz & {z}^{2}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[\\frac{∂}{∂y}({z}^{2})-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(xz)]i-[\\frac{∂}{∂x}({z}^{2})-\\frac{∂}{∂z}({x}^{2})]j+[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xz)-\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2})]k \\\\  & =(0-x)i-(0-0)j+(z-0)k \\\\  & =-x\\,i+z\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate $\\text{curl}\\,F$ at the point $(-2,-3,1),$ and obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\text{curl}\\,F)(-2,-3,1) & =-(-2)\\,i+(1)\\,k \\\\  & =2\\,i+\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045767/state.json" "file_sha256" "e834a2341c6e1f18464a75d5fa46289659b30f3fc44107666214c011a5735328"} {"question" "q-131340" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045767/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4dec808fbb78198391326e2601a173f95510b8bd3afbddce4d593ffa6479681a"} {"question" "q-131340" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045767/state.json" "file_sha256" "e834a2341c6e1f18464a75d5fa46289659b30f3fc44107666214c011a5735328"} {"question" "q-131340" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\,i-2\\,k"] ["math" "2\\,i+\\,k"] ["math" "2\\,j-3\\,k"] ["math" "3\\,i+\\,j"] ["math" "\\,j+\\,k"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045767/state.json" "file_sha256" "e834a2341c6e1f18464a75d5fa46289659b30f3fc44107666214c011a5735328"} {"question" "q-131340" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2\\,i+\\,k"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045767/state.json" "file_sha256" "e834a2341c6e1f18464a75d5fa46289659b30f3fc44107666214c011a5735328"} {"question" "q-105668" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $F(x,y,z)=3{z}^{2}\\,i+2y\\,j+k,$ what is $\\text{curl}\\,F?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045767/state.json" "file_sha256" "e834a2341c6e1f18464a75d5fa46289659b30f3fc44107666214c011a5735328"} {"question" "q-105668" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j+R\\,k$ is a vector field on ${R}^{3}$ and the partial derivatives of the components of $F$ all exist, then the curl of $F$ is the vector field given by\n\n$$\ncurl\\,F=∇\\times F=|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ P & Q & R\\end{aligned}|.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{curl}\\,F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ 3{z}^{2} & 2y & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[\\frac{∂}{∂y}(1)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(2y)]i-[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(1)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(3{z}^{2})]j+[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2y)-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3{z}^{2})]k \\\\  & =(0-0)i-(0-6z)j+(0-0)k \\\\  & =6z\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045767/state.json" "file_sha256" "e834a2341c6e1f18464a75d5fa46289659b30f3fc44107666214c011a5735328"} {"question" "q-105668" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045767/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4dec808fbb78198391326e2601a173f95510b8bd3afbddce4d593ffa6479681a"} {"question" "q-105668" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045767/state.json" "file_sha256" "e834a2341c6e1f18464a75d5fa46289659b30f3fc44107666214c011a5735328"} {"question" "q-105668" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-6z\\,j+2\\,\\text{k}"] ["math" "-6z\\,k"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "2\\,i"] ["math" "6z\\,j"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045767/state.json" "file_sha256" "e834a2341c6e1f18464a75d5fa46289659b30f3fc44107666214c011a5735328"} {"question" "q-105668" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6z\\,j"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045767/state.json" "file_sha256" "e834a2341c6e1f18464a75d5fa46289659b30f3fc44107666214c011a5735328"} {"question" "q-126529" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the vector field $F(x,y)=(2x+{y}^{2})\\,i+y{e}^{x}\\,j.$ Evaluate the scalar curl of $F$ at the point $(1,1).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045767/state.json" "file_sha256" "e834a2341c6e1f18464a75d5fa46289659b30f3fc44107666214c011a5735328"} {"question" "q-126529" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}$ and the partial derivatives of the components of $F$ all exist, then the *scalar* curl of $F$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y{e}^{x})-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2x+{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =y{e}^{x}-2y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the scalar curl at the point $(1,1),$ and obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})}_{(1,1)} & =(1){e}^{1}-2(1) \\\\  & =e-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045767/state.json" "file_sha256" "e834a2341c6e1f18464a75d5fa46289659b30f3fc44107666214c011a5735328"} {"question" "q-126529" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045767/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4dec808fbb78198391326e2601a173f95510b8bd3afbddce4d593ffa6479681a"} {"question" "q-126529" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045767/state.json" "file_sha256" "e834a2341c6e1f18464a75d5fa46289659b30f3fc44107666214c011a5735328"} {"question" "q-126529" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2e"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "2e+1"] ["math" "e-2"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045767/state.json" "file_sha256" "e834a2341c6e1f18464a75d5fa46289659b30f3fc44107666214c011a5735328"} {"question" "q-126529" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "e-2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045767/state.json" "file_sha256" "e834a2341c6e1f18464a75d5fa46289659b30f3fc44107666214c011a5735328"} {"question" "q-126525" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the vector field $F(x,y)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)\\,i+(x{y}^{2}+1)\\,j.$ Evaluate the scalar curl of $F$ at the point $(0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045767/state.json" "file_sha256" "e834a2341c6e1f18464a75d5fa46289659b30f3fc44107666214c011a5735328"} {"question" "q-126525" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}$ and the partial derivatives of the components of $F$ all exist, then the *scalar* curl of $F$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x{y}^{2}+1)-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)) \\\\  & ={y}^{2}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the scalar curl at the point $(0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}),$ and obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})}_{(0,\\pi /2)} & ={(\\frac{\\pi }{2})}^{2}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0+\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{4}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045767/state.json" "file_sha256" "e834a2341c6e1f18464a75d5fa46289659b30f3fc44107666214c011a5735328"} {"question" "q-126525" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045767/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4dec808fbb78198391326e2601a173f95510b8bd3afbddce4d593ffa6479681a"} {"question" "q-126525" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045767/state.json" "file_sha256" "e834a2341c6e1f18464a75d5fa46289659b30f3fc44107666214c011a5735328"} {"question" "q-126525" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "2{\\pi }^{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{4}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045767/state.json" "file_sha256" "e834a2341c6e1f18464a75d5fa46289659b30f3fc44107666214c011a5735328"} {"question" "q-126525" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{4}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045767/state.json" "file_sha256" "e834a2341c6e1f18464a75d5fa46289659b30f3fc44107666214c011a5735328"} {"question" "q-126544" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $F(x,y)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,i+{e}^{xy}\\,j,$ what is the scalar curl of $F?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045767/state.json" "file_sha256" "e834a2341c6e1f18464a75d5fa46289659b30f3fc44107666214c011a5735328"} {"question" "q-126544" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}$ and the partial derivatives of the components of $F$ all exist, then the *scalar* curl of $F$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{xy})-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡y) \\\\  & =y{e}^{xy}-(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y) \\\\  & =y{e}^{xy}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡y.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-ca